From f4c6bb4a7e04e3441092467b1b491a4b924efe5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arch-port <26345330+DrShadow34@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 11:11:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] panvk: v9 geometry shaders through src/poly

Mali has no geometry stage. Mesa's common emulation (src/poly, from
Asahi, as Honeykrisp) on the v9 job manager:

- the vertex shader feeding a geometry shader gets a compute variant
  (PANVK_VS_VARIANT_SW) storing its outputs to memory; attributes through
  load_attribute_pan with the invocation's vertex / instance ID (allowed
  in compute on v9+), the index buffer pulled in the shader;
- the geometry shader compiles to a hardware vertex shader run once per
  output vertex (PANVK_GS_VARIANT_RAST, first variant: it is the hardware
  VS the fragment shader links with) and, for dynamic topologies, a
  compute shader writing the index buffer (PANVK_GS_VARIANT_MAIN);
- per draw, the two compute jobs go into the vertex/tiler chain ahead of
  the IDVS job, which draws poly's shape (indexed with restarts, static
  index buffer or instanced lists / strips) and depends on them; poly's
  vertex / geometry parameters are sysvals;
- 64-wide workgroups, invocations past poly's grid return early (Mali
  compute jobs count workgroups);
- the geometry shader has the compute driver set (dummy sampler, dynamic
  buffers) and its own resource table; meta saves / restores it.

Not done: indirect draws and primitive restart in strips with a geometry
shader (poly's GPU-side setup), transform feedback, adjacency without a
geometry shader; those draws are skipped with a warning.

CTS geometry.*: 188 pass, 1 fail (primitive restart), 10 skip.

